Given a ring $R$, its centroid $Z(R)$, and an ideal $I$ in $R$ such that $I$ is within the centroid, we define the enveloping numbers $\overline{
u}_i(R)$ for every non-negative integer $i$. These overbar numbers $\overline{
u}_i(R)$ correspond to the sequence of numbers $
u_i(R)$ for the ring $R/Z(R)-I$, where the ring $R/Z(R)$ is considered an enlarged version of the ring $R$ with a unity added through the centroid $Z(R)$. Enveloping numbers play a pivotal role in understanding the structure of finite rings by providing essential insights. In this paper, we calculate the overbar numbers $
u_i(R)$ for specific types of rings, namely group rings and upper triangular matrix rings. In the course of this investigation, we also derive the overbar numbers $
u_i(R)$ for a wide class of finite rings with a low nilpotency index. Additionally, we establish a formula for computing the overbar numbers $
u_i(R)$ in a wide class of finite rings with a low nilpotency index and derive the envelope numbers $\overline{
u}_i(R)$, which in turn helps in classifying finite rings based on the value of $\overline{
u}_i(R)$.
